JSON Schema compares numbers by value, so an enum member written as a
float with no fractional part, such as 1.0, is also an integer.

The output is wrong: such members are dropped next to an integer type,
leaving no members at all for direct and allOf.

-- schema.json --
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "type": "object",
  "$defs": {
    "int": {"type": "integer"}
  },
  "properties": {
    "direct": {"type": "integer", "enum": [1.0, 2.5]},
    "allOf": {"type": "integer", "allOf": [{"enum": [1.0, 2.0]}]},
    "ref": {"$ref": "#/$defs/int", "allOf": [{"enum": [1.0, 2.0]}]}
  }
}
-- test/err-direct-integral.json --
{"direct": 1}
-- test/err-allof-integral.json --
{"allOf": 2}
-- test/ok-ref-integral.json --
{"ref": 1}
-- test/err-direct.json --
{"direct": 3}
-- test/err-allof.json --
{"allOf": 3}
-- test/err-ref.json --
{"ref": 3}
-- out/decode/extract --
@jsonschema(schema="https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema")
direct?: error("disallowed")
allOf?:  error("disallowed")
ref?:    #int & (==1.0 | ==2.0)

#int: int
...
-- out/decode/testerr/err-allof-integral --
allOf: disallowed:
    generated.cue:3:10
-- out/decode/testerr/err-allof --
allOf: disallowed:
    generated.cue:3:10
-- out/decode/testerr/err-direct-integral --
direct: disallowed:
    generated.cue:2:10
-- out/decode/testerr/err-direct --
direct: disallowed:
    generated.cue:2:10
-- out/decode/testerr/err-ref --
ref: 2 errors in empty disjunction:
ref: invalid value 3 (out of bound ==1.0):
    generated.cue:4:18
    generated.cue:4:10
    test/err-ref.json:1:9
ref: invalid value 3 (out of bound ==2.0):
    generated.cue:4:26
    generated.cue:4:10
    test/err-ref.json:1:9
